#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# vector_around

#% text
# `vector_around(v, [s1, ...])` is the vector `v` with independent standard uncertainties `si`; `vector_around(v, c)` is the vector with the covariance matrix `c`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# `vector_around(v, [[s1, ...], r])` gives every two entries the correlation `r`, `vector_around(v, [[s1, ...], R])` the correlation matrix `R`; both are kept as the covariance matrix.

#% item
# `around_replace` takes it for a list of variables.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
vector_around([1.8, 2.4], [0.3, 0.4])
#% output
#= vector_around([1.8, 2.4], [0.3, 0.4])

#% cell
vector_around([1.8, 2.4], [[0.3, 0.4], 0.5])
#% output
#= vector_around([1.8, 2.4], [[0.09, 0.06], [0.06, 0.16000000000000003]])

#% cell
vector_around([1, 2], [[1/10, 1/5], [[1, 1/2], [1/2, 1]]])
#% output
#= vector_around([1, 2], [[1/100, 1/100], [1/100, 1/25]])

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `around`, `around_replace`
